{"term":"arrow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:625fc7e4e7cbf97b64","definition":"A projectile consisting of a shaft, a point and a tail with stabilizing fins that is shot from a bow.","example":"The Citizens in their rage, imagining that euery poſt in the Churche had bin one of yᵉ Souldyers, ſhot habbe or nabbe at randon^([sic – meaning random]) uppe to the Roode lofte, and to the Chancell, leauing ſome of theyr arrowes ſticking in the Images.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["streal"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arrow arum","arrowback","arrow bag","arrow bamboo","arrow board","arrow crab","arrow-finger","arrowgrass","arrow-head","arrowhead","arrowheaded","arrow-hole","arrow in the quiver","arrowleaf","arrowless","arrowlet","arrowlike","arrowmaker","arrow of love","arrow of time","time's arrow","arrow paradox","arrowpoint","arrow point","arrow poison","arrow-poison frog","arrow prayer","arrowproof","arrow-root","arrowroot"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:497ac584791a254301","definition":"A sign or symbol used to indicate a direction (e.g.→).","example":"Consider now the arrow with initial point A and terminal point B; this arrow we shall designate by #92;overrightarrow#123;AB#125;. If a#95;1,a#95;2,a#95;3, and b#95;1,b#95;2,b#95;3 are the coordinates of A and B, respectively, then #92;overrightarrow#123;AB#125; is equal to the arrow #92;overrightarrow#123;OP#125;, where O is the origin of the coordinate system and P has coordinates b#95;1-a#95;1,b#95;2-a#95;2,b#95;3-a#95;3. Thus each arrow is equal to one having the origin as its initial point.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["arrow arum","arrowback","arrow bag","arrow bamboo","arrow board","arrow crab","arrow-finger","arrowgrass","arrow-head","arrowhead","arrowh